<h2>Terms</h2>
<p>These are the terms you agree to when you buy something from
{{ business }}{% if address %}, {{ address }}{% endif %}.</p>

<h3>Prices and payment</h3>
<p>Prices are shown{% if currency %} in {{ currency }}{% endif %} on the page you
buy from, and that is what you pay. Any tax is worked out at checkout. Payment is
taken by Stripe on their own secure page &mdash; your card details never reach
this website.</p>

<h3>What you get</h3>
{% if sells_physical %}<p>Physical items are sent to the address you give at
checkout. We will tell you if anything is delayed.</p>{% endif %}
{% if sells_digital %}<p>Downloads are available immediately after payment,
through a link we email you. Keep that email &mdash; it is how you get back to
your files.</p>{% endif %}
{% if sells_services %}<p>Sessions are booked through the link we email you, at
times we have available. Each booking uses one session.</p>{% endif %}

<h3>Cancelling</h3>
<p>See <a href="{{ refunds_href }}">{{ refunds_title }}</a> for when you can
change your mind and how refunds work.</p>

<h3>If we cannot deliver</h3>
<p>If we cannot supply something you have paid for, we will tell you and refund
you in full. That is the limit of what we owe you, except where the law says
otherwise &mdash; nothing here removes rights you have by law.</p>

<h3>Getting in touch</h3>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ email }}">{{ email }}</a>. We answer as quickly as we
can, and always within a few working days.</p>
{% if governing_law %}
<h3>Which law applies</h3>
<p>These terms are governed by the law of {{ governing_law }}. If you are buying
as a consumer, you keep the protection of the law where you live.</p>
{% endif %}
